ity, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's see each candidate:\n\nA: strong technical (anticipate dangerous, complex connections, spatial vision), leadership, but concerns: unorganized, not good at criticism (adaptability), maybe reliability? Not mentioned. No stress resilience evidence. Cooperation? Not mentioned.\n\nB: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). No mention of decision quality.\n\nC: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation), can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Good reliability.\n\nD: takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), can concentrate well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), responds adequately to unexpected events (stress resilience), but arrogant (cooperation), weak leadership (crew cooperation). No mention of reliability.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate D has many strengths but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A has technical strengths but organizational and criticism issues.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall, despite communication issues, but we need to discuss. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference that no prior discussion, so we can start by stating recommendation and evidence.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
